11. The Complete Pre-Ship Native Verification Gate (Zero Guesswork)

Run every screen, custom engine, or component against this 12-point diagnostic
before shipping:

1.  Hierarchy Check: Does content fill the screen edge-to-edge while functional
    chrome floats distinctly above it? (Zero fake boxes wrapping every section;
    zero glass stacked on glass.)
2.  Optical Geometry Check: Are all corners true continuous squircles
    (kCACornerCurveContinuous) with concentric nested corner subtraction
    (r_inner = max(r_outer - d, 0)), and asymmetric glyphs optically shifted
    toward centroid?
3.  Shader / Material Check: Is saturation applied before blur, dynamic range
    compressed via floor + ceiling (min/max), rim stroked with two concentric
    directional passes (0.5pt + 1.0pt), and scroll edges softly
    variable-blurred?
4.  Physics Check: Are all animations velocity-preserving ODE springs (bounce /
    duration)—zero ease-in-out defaults, zero teleporting values, exact 0.998/ms
    scroll friction + 0.55 rubber-banding?
5.  Interruption Check: Can every sheet, zoom transition, and drawer be grabbed,
    reversed, or retargeted cleanly mid-flight without freezing or losing state?
6.  Pacing Check: Does the loop run locked to targetPresentationTimestamp across
    discrete LTPO buckets (120/80/60/48...) with atomic Metal/CA commits?
7.  Typography Check: Are opsz optical cutovers (20pt), size-specific tracking,
    linear-space blending + stem darkening, and 672pt readable line caps all
    active?
8.  Color & Display Check: Is wide-gamut Display P3 + thermal-aware EDR headroom
    used only on true accents/glows while resting dark surfaces step luminance
    smoothly (#000 -> #1C1C1E -> #2C2C2E)?
9.  Tactile & Sound Check: Do transients fire < 10ms locked to physical
    snap/contact points, pass the "100th-use non-annoyance test", and respect
    the hardware Mute switch?
10. Ergonomics & Copy Check: Are all touch targets >= 44×44pt (60×60pt
    visionOS), hairlines physical 1px, capitalization strictly split Title vs.
    Sentence case, and alert buttons named by explicit consequence verbs?
11. Accessibility Stress Check: Does the screen survive AX5 Giant Text
    (horizontal \to vertical reflow), VoiceOver (grouped cards), Reduce Motion
    (cross-fade fallback), Reduce Transparency (>= 4.5:1 solid fallback), and
    Color-Blind Grayscale?
12. Native Idiom Check: If you hide the app logo, does the iOS version feel
    unmistakably iOS, the Mac version unmistakably Mac, and zero foreign
    Android/web idioms leak through?
